---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Giscus from '../../components/Giscus.astro';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<Layout
  title="SoloMD Settings Reference — Every Option Explained"
  description="A complete tour of SoloMD's Settings: settings search with step-to-match, first-line tab titles, missing-file save check, auto-numbering headings, pasted image width, Writer shortcut preset, E2EE cloud sync, and one-click updates."
  lang={lang}
>
  <Header lang={lang} />
  <main id="main">
    <article class="container docs-article">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs">
        <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/docs/">Docs</a> / <span>Settings</span>
      </nav>

      <h1>Settings Reference</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Press <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + ,</kbd> to open Settings. Use the search bar at the top to filter any setting or shortcut by keyword, and click the <kbd>⌵</kbd> button next to the search box to step through matches with a visible pulse highlight.
      </p>

      <h2>1. General &amp; File Safety</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Use first line of document as tab title</strong> (off by default): displays the first non-empty line of the document (skipping YAML front-matter) in the tab bar instead of the filename — ideal for notes opened with temporary or UUID filenames.</li>
        <li><strong>Check if original file exists before saving</strong> (off by default): designed for editing temporary files opened by third-party software. When enabled, if the original file on disk has been deleted or cleaned up externally, background auto-save is skipped and manual save (<kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + S</kbd>) asks for confirmation before recreating the file.</li>
        <li><strong>Automatically number 1–6 headings</strong> (off by default): keeps hierarchical section numbers (<code>1 / 1.1 / 1.1.1</code>) updated automatically whenever headings are added, deleted, or modified.</li>
        <li><strong>Read-only file Save As guard</strong>: attempting to save a read-only file warns you and opens “Save As” pre-filled with <code>&lt;name&gt;-copy.md</code>, and closing a modified read-only tab always prompts first.</li>
        <li><strong>Restore session &amp; per-workspace tabs</strong>: reopens your tabs and exact viewport scroll positions on launch; each workspace folder remembers its own tab set independently.</li>
        <li><strong>Auto-reload external changes</strong>: clean tabs reload automatically when updated on disk by external tools (Syncthing, Git); dirty tabs always ask before overwriting your edits.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Writing &amp; Editor</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Word wrap, line numbers, active-line highlight, and readable column width limit</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Always show Markdown syntax markers</strong>: keeps <code>**</code>, <code>#</code>, and other markers visible at all times so lines never shift when moving the caret.</li>
        <li><strong>Pasted image destination &amp; default width</strong>: choose shared <code>_assets/</code>, per-note <code>.assets/</code>, or Typora-compatible <code>./images/$&#123;filename&#125;/</code> templates; set a default width preset for pasted images and resize any image from the right-click menu.</li>
        <li><strong>Code block wrap, line numbers &amp; language suggestions</strong>: soft-wrap long lines in code fences and toggle language autocomplete when typing <code>```</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Vim mode, Focus mode (<kbd>F8</kbd>), Typewriter mode (<kbd>F9</kbd>), and non-blinking solid cursor</strong>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Appearance &amp; Custom Themes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Theme</strong>: Light, Dark, or <strong>Follow OS appearance</strong>, plus built-in community themes like Ivory Amber.</li>
        <li><strong>Custom CSS &amp; DevTools</strong>: write rules in <code>custom.css</code> and click “Open DevTools” (or press <kbd>F12</kbd>) to inspect live DOM elements. Active custom themes and CSS are also inlined automatically into HTML and PDF exports.</li>
        <li><strong>Fonts &amp; independent font sizes</strong>: configure separate prose and code fonts, independent editor / UI / preview font sizes, and whole-app zoom (<kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + +/−/0</kbd>) with a centered percentage HUD. On Android, you can also load local font files from <code>/storage/emulated/0/Fonts</code>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Shortcuts &amp; Writer Preset</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Click the <strong>“Writer (Typora / Word)” preset</strong> at the top of <em>Settings → Shortcuts</em> to bind <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + B</kbd> to Bold (moving Toggle File Tree to <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Shift + B</kbd>).</li>
        <li>All 60+ commands are individually rebindable, and native menus reflect your active bindings immediately.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Sync, History, AI &amp; Grammar Check</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Sync</strong>: WebDAV E2EE Sync, Local Cloud Drive Encrypted Vault Folder, Direct Cloud Drive OpenAPI Sync, and GitHub Sync (see the <a href="/docs/sync/">Sync &amp; History guide</a>).</li>
        <li><strong>Language &amp; Check</strong>: built-in spellcheck, CJK proofreading, and optional <strong>LanguageTool grammar &amp; style checking</strong> (public API or self-hosted server).</li>
        <li><strong>AI</strong>: 14+ BYOK cloud providers and local Ollama (see <a href="/docs/ai/">AI features</a>). All API keys and cloud tokens are stored in the OS keychain.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. In-App One-Click Update Installer</h2>
      <p>
        Clicking the update button in <em>Settings → About</em> (or the header update pill) downloads the native installer for your platform and architecture with live progress and launches it automatically, with automatic GitHub / Gitee mirror fallback for users in mainland China.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Resetting to Defaults</h2>
      <p>
        To reset all settings to factory defaults, quit SoloMD and delete the app data directory — <code>%APPDATA%\app.solomd</code> on Windows (or the <code>data/</code> folder next to <code>SoloMD.exe</code> in portable mode), <code>~/Library/Application Support/app.solomd</code> on macOS, or <code>~/.config/app.solomd</code> on Linux. Your notes are ordinary files elsewhere and are never touched.
      </p>

      <Giscus />
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer lang={lang} />
</Layout>
